## Summary
**Hide the simulated wallet** (`src/web/index.html`). It doesn't buy anything, so it's hidden behind `SHOW_SIM = false`:
- the "Simulated wallet" menu entry; `/sim` now redirects to `/explore`;
- on Launches, the "Bought (simulated)" tile and the "Bought (sim)" tab;
- the "bought (sim)" / "pass, no buy" labels in the Scanner column and on the token page, which now read just "gates pass";
- the "Simulated trade" line on evaluation pages;
- the "Simulated wallet" block in Settings.

The worker and the API are unchanged; set `SHOW_SIM = true` to bring it back.

**Big On-chain analysis button** on token pages: a gradient call-to-action with an icon, placed under the header with a one-line description of what the analysis covers. It replaces the small text link and goes full width on phones.

**AI models** (`src/config.js`, `.env.example`, README):
- the scanner's AI analyst and group reviews default to `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5` (`NEAR_AI_MODEL`);
- only the On-chain analysis write-up keeps `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5` (`NEAR_AI_ANALYSIS_MODEL`).

**Deploy note:** set `NEAR_AI_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5` on the host (or remove it so the new default applies).

## Test plan
- [x] `npm test` (31 pass)
- [x] Browser, public mode, live data:
  - the Launches page shows no sim tile, tab or labels, and the menu has no Simulated wallet;
  - `/sim` lands on `/explore`;
  - the THREE token page shows the big button, which opens `/analysis/<token>`;
  - the button was also checked in light theme and at mobile width (full width, 50 px tall).
- [x] Haiku 5.5 through NEAR AI:
  - `check-ai` ok;
  - scanner analyst dry run on ABC: SELL 0.80, high risk, `claude-haiku-5-5`;
  - group review of `c_40e4da7e`: 7.1 s, neutral 0.35 (not saved).
- [x] Config resolves to Haiku for the scanner and group reviews, and to Sonnet for the On-chain analysis

